<title>FRANCE: Moroccan operators bought 25-50,000 T U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Moroccan operators bought 25-50,000 T U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Moroccan operators recently bought between 25,000 and 50,000 tonnes of U.S. soft red winter wheat for July delivery at around $137.50-138 per tonne cost and freight, European grain exporters said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>There was no official confirmation of the deal. But exporters said it was hard to track private business unleashed by the liberalisation of the Moroccan grain markets.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
